course: dictionary
lesson: 5336
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Khan» is one of them. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. You can check by swapping in your idea and asking if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Temujin united the Mongol tribes and in 1206 was named Genghis Khan, meaning universal ruler.» The sentence says the name means universal ruler, so here a khan is a ruler or king of the Mongols and other peoples of Central Asia.
explain: Look at «Genghis Khan» and «Kublai Khan». These are names, but the word before «Khan» is a person's own name, not a family name. Khan was a title that came before or after a ruler's name, and it was never just a surname in those times.
explain: Today, Khan is also a common family name in South Asia and elsewhere. A footballer, mayor or cricketer called Khan is using it as a surname, not as a title for a king.
fact: A khan was a ruler or king among the Mongols, Turks and other peoples of Central Asia.
fact: Genghis Khan united the Mongol tribes and built the largest land empire the world had seen.
fact: Kublai Khan was Genghis Khan's grandson, and he became emperor of China.
fact: Khan is a common family name today in South Asia and elsewhere.
fact: Long ago, a khan could also mean an inn where travelling merchants and their camels stayed on old trade routes such as the Silk Road.
exercise: In «Temujin ... was named Genghis Khan, meaning universal ruler», what does Khan mean? | A tribe that lived by the sea | *A ruler or king | A river in Asia | A kind of camel
exercise: «Marco Polo said he served Kublai Khan for 17 years.» Which country did Kublai Khan rule? | *China | Italy | Egypt | Scotland
exercise: Today «Khan» is used as a family name. What does this tell you? | *Many people share it as a surname | It is always a royal title | It means an old inn | It is a kind of camel
test: Long ago, a khan was also an inn where travelling merchants and their camels stayed. In that sense, what was a khan? | A kind of bridge over a valley | *A place where merchants stayed | A palace for a king | A river crossing
test: Which name is a ruler, not just a family name? | Kublai the Venetian | Marco Polo | Babur the traveller | *Kublai Khan
exam: In the words «Genghis Khan», what kind of word is Khan, and what does it tell you? | A type of food, meaning dinner | A word that means a long journey | A river in the mountains | *A title meaning ruler, used as part of a name
